{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id227014488"}, "name":{"label":"Mito Ming Ming"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2024-09-12T00:30:12-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"2"}, "im:version":{"label":"6.0.3"}, "id":{"label":"11715247656"}, "title":{"label":"Great app BUT!"}, "content":{"label":"Everything but the core function of the app is great - the design, CARROT’s subtle death threats, and the customisation that comes with it. But the accuracy for the forecast throughout the day, let alone the week, is really really terrible. I understand that the maker has nothing to do with the source, and I am not blaming them, but the source has proven completely unreliable continually over the last year. I love the app, but I put functionality above all other features (with great difficulty), and cannot find myself using this app to check the weather. Please focus your attention on this issue.\n\nUpdate. The app’s accuracy has worsened, and moreover, it’s inconsistent with its own data. It’s one thing to have incorrect data pulled from a source, but it’s another thing to have your display read “UV index of 4 on Sunday” when the UV index graph says the peak is on Saturday, and Sunday is an index of 2. I don’t think I’ll ever uninstall the app, but I’d rather say something that not.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=961390574&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
